    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="edfb9aa9-9d46-50af-aa9d-98d24c84ccbd" activityNameId="c52e88f8-b999-50f8-a741-7afe25305972" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, hard coal ash, 0% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, hard coal ash, 0% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% FR hard coal ash; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 540660; H n.a.; C n.a.; S 2629.4; N n.a.; P 1026.8; B 219.46; Cl 35.935; Br 39.825; F 82.318; I 2.7918; Ag n.a.; As 50.08; Ba 1494.4; Cd 0.81967; Co 39.332; Cr 148.13; Cu 74.111; Hg 0.13533; Mn 429.54; Mo 12.58; Ni 112.38; Pb 132.49; Sb 14.047; Se 10.231; Sn 34.465; V 211.82; Zn 631.72; Be 13.254; Sc 41.949; Sr 1515.5; Ti 6333.1; Tl 6.5216; W 17.367; Si 185270; Fe 52187; Ca 14819; Al 126300; K 14737; Mg 43325; Na 7345.1; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 60.4%. ;; UUID: 7a352cc1-4491-4024-8451-c8d5437c68e3
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. 
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7a352cc1-4491-4024-8451-c8d5437c68e3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
